{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791219306,"nonce":"U2UOjxMwgCPg8mASDbkcmoaD/lk=","title":"Every array store took a global mutex and a runtime call","message":"Found from the new Benchmarks Game kernels (fannkuchredux 2.2 s at n=10, Cranelift and LLVM equal, i.e. not a codegen gap).\n\n1. `arr[i] = v` lowered to a call to haxe_array_set_i64/_f64 (field/lvalue.rs), which for any 8-byte-slot array called `bytes_data_set` -\u003e `bytes_data_source` -\u003e `BYTES_DATA_VIEWS.lock()` + HashMap lookup (added 72390210 for Bytes.getData() views). Every Bytes.set/setInt32/blit (`sync_bytes_data_views`, iterating the whole map) and every haxe_bytes_free (a `retain` over the map) took the same lock. Programs with no getData() view paid it all.\n2. Reads were already inline (`lower_index_access`), stores were not.\n\nFix:\n- BYTES_DATA_VIEW_COUNT (atomic, written under the lock) lets every view path skip the lock while no view exists.\n- HaxeArray gains a `flags` word (40-byte header; MIR allocations in literals.rs / construction.rs, stdlib/array.rs wrappers, rayzor-tensors shape arrays updated); getData()/ofData() mark the array HAXE_ARRAY_VIEW.\n- Array stores go inline when `idx \u003c len \u0026\u0026 flags == 0`, else through the runtime setter (growth, null array, views).\n\nnuc A/B (benchmark_runner, min ms, base = bb3283ec):\n  fannkuchredux llvm 2185 -\u003e 237, cranelift 2253 -\u003e 343\n  pidigits      llvm  905 -\u003e 221, cranelift  940 -\u003e 414\n  revcomp       llvm   92 -\u003e  71, cranelift  103 -\u003e  85\n  fasta, mandelbrot -1..-3%; knucleotide +2..3% (noise band); nbody, spectralnorm, fibonacci, deltablue, binarytrees unchanged.\nThe runtime lock alone (step 1) gave fannkuchredux 2188 -\u003e 752, pidigits 906 -\u003e 354.\n\nGate on the nuc vs nbase: conformance 690 -\u003e 690 no row moved; BytesDataViews regression OK; suite 206/0/2 where the extra crash is test_exception in a run started right after conformance (a0912d8; 10/10 standalone passes); integration 830 passed; runtime lib 84, compiler lib 742; clippy (runtime, compiler, rayzor-tensors) clean; 4 examples pass. All 7 kernels still byte-identical to haxe --interp.","files":null}]}